.TH OMAROLL 1 "" "Omaroll" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
omaroll \- photo, video and PDF viewer and library for Omarchy
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B omaroll
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fIfile\fR ... | \fIfolder\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Pictures and videos open in the viewer, which steps through the rest of their
folder in name order. Multiple files open as a selection in the supplied order.
A folder, a PDF, or no argument at all opens the library. Use
.B \-\-
before filenames that begin with a dash.
.PP
Press
.B ?
or
.B F1
in the library or the viewer, with no sheet or menu open, for the shortcuts
that apply there.
Omaroll never moves, copies or changes your files unless you ask it to rename
them, move them to Trash or save a corrected copy. The exception is
.BR Shift+Delete ,
which deletes permanently. It asks first, unless that confirmation is turned
off in Settings.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-library
Open files in the library instead of the viewer. The file is selected and its
folder is added to the library if it is not already watched.
.TP
.BI \-\-start " time"
Start the request's first video at seconds, mm:ss or hh:mm:ss (fractions
allowed). Overrides the saved resume position. A time that can't be read
exits with status 2, with the reason on stderr and as a desktop notice.
.TP
.BR \-\-set\-default " [" \fIgroup\fR ]
Use Omaroll for a group of file types:
.BR images ,
.BR videos ,
.BR pdf ,
or
.B all
(images and videos, the default). Prints what changed and how to undo it, and,
while Omaroll's Hyprland window rules are not installed or turned down, the
command that installs them. Add
.B \-\-verbose
to list every type.
.TP
.BR \-\-unset\-default " [" \fIgroup\fR ]
Put back the apps
.B \-\-set\-default
replaced. Name the same group:
.B omaroll \-\-unset\-default pdf
undoes
.BR "omaroll \-\-set\-default pdf" .
Each line of
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/mimeapps.list
(\fI~/.config/mimeapps.list\fR when
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is unset or empty) goes back as it was, and what Omaroll added is removed,
including a section or file that was not there before, so the file is
unchanged after any number of set and unset cycles. The exceptions: Omaroll is
taken out of that file for the group's types wherever it is named, so an
Added Associations entry naming it goes too (Removed Associations entries
stay); it is also taken out of the desktop's own list beside it, such as
.IR hyprland\-mimeapps.list ,
and of the lists in
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/applications
(\fI~/.local/share/applications\fR), and nothing in those is put back; and an
app chosen after
.B \-\-set\-default
stays. Types with nothing of yours to put back keep their system default, and
the summary counts them.
.TP
.B \-\-install\-window\-rules
Add Omaroll's Hyprland rules to
.IR ~/.config/hypr :
full opacity for its windows and a floating viewer. Needs Omarchy's Lua
Hyprland config. Settings has the same choice. A second viewer opened on the
same workspace tiles with the first on purpose, so the two are not stacked.
Each Omaroll does this for its own viewers. Normally one Omaroll holds them
all; a second one started on its own arranges its viewers separately.
.TP
.B \-\-remove\-window\-rules
Take those rules out again, leaving
.I hyprland.lua
as it was before. A line that only requires hypr.omaroll goes too; any other
line that loads the rules is reported and left for you to edit. A rules file
you wrote yourself is kept.
.TP
.B \-\-diagnostics
Print the versions, graphics and optional tools that a bug report needs, and
exit. No window opens. This is the same text as Copy diagnostics in Settings.
.TP
.B \-\-demo
Browse a deterministic fictional library instead of your own files. Nothing
personal appears on screen.
.TP
.BI \-\-render " file.png"
Render the window to a PNG and exit. Draws offscreen, so no compositor can
resize it or overlap it. Fails without writing if the view never becomes
ready.
.TP
.BI \-\-render\-view " view"
Which view to render: grid, detail, document, video, slideshow, matte,
corrections, compare, export, rename, ocr, editors, pins, context-menu,
selection-menu, duplicates, similar, browser, sidebar, settings, viewer,
viewer-video, viewer-info, viewer-menu, viewer-help or grid-filenames.
.TP
.BI \-\-render\-size " WxH"
Window size, from 560x420 (viewer 320x240) to 7680x4320. Default 1280x820.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-help ", " \-h
Show a summary of the options.
.SH EXAMPLES
Open pictures and videos with Omaroll from the file manager, then undo it:
.PP
.RS
.nf
omaroll \-\-set\-default
omaroll \-\-unset\-default
.fi
.RE
.PP
View a picture and step through its folder, or browse a folder:
.PP
.RS
.nf
omaroll photo.jpg
omaroll ~/Pictures
.fi
.RE
.PP
Play a video from 1 minute 23 seconds:
.PP
.RS
.nf
omaroll \-\-start=1:23 clip.mp4
.fi
.RE
.PP
Render the demo library's similar pictures to a PNG:
.PP
.RS
.nf
omaroll \-\-render similar.png \-\-render\-view similar
.fi
.RE
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B OMARCHY_SCREENSHOT_EDITOR
The annotation editor. Tensaku when unset.
.TP
.B OMARCHY_OCR_LANGS
Tesseract languages for text in pictures, joined with +. Default eng.
.TP
.B QT_IMAGEIO_MAXALLOC
The most memory, in megabytes, one picture may use.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/omaroll
Settings, albums, tags, favourites and saved views;
.I ~/.config/omaroll
when
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is unset.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/omaroll/mime\-defaults.ini
What
.B \-\-set\-default
replaced, for
.B \-\-unset\-default
to put back. A record in
.I ~/.config/Omaroll
from an older version moves here on the next run.
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/omaroll
Thumbnails, the cover art a playing video shows in player controls, and the
text, date and similarity caches;
.I ~/.cache/omaroll
when
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
is unset. Safe to delete.
.TP
.I /usr/share/omaroll/hypr/omaroll.lua
The Hyprland window rules that
.B \-\-install\-window\-rules
copies into
.IR ~/.config/hypr ,
as the Arch package installs them. A source build puts them under its own
prefix, /usr/local/share by default.
.SH BUGS
Report problems at https://github.com/btsouth/omaroll/issues with the output of
.BR "omaroll \-\-diagnostics" .
.SH SEE ALSO
https://btsouth.github.io/omaroll/
